{
	"nodes":[
		{
			"id":"487c105b27d937a7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Who is Yahweh?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-600,
			"y":-120,
			"width":160,
			"height":60
		},
		{"id":"7e14b626b3c027e9","type":"link","url":"https://youtu.be/JIMAqxGPR8Q?si=_jeTki5CxuuHT8Yb","x":-840,"y":-10,"width":400,"height":120},
		{
			"id":"40440872cc287837",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Leviticus",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-2930,
			"width":140,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"e63e3622c0934d0d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The introduction of Yahweh",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-300,
			"y":-3200,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"7fe1c69e21ef9df6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"A Physical God\n(the Old Testament)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-300,
			"y":-3120,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ce9431a4647810e6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Satan first mentioned",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-300,
			"y":-3020,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4dc5c38664643691",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The one who set that set himself up as god",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-5840,
			"width":340,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"8ea53b2b95df7a36",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The one that tried to overthrow the kingdom",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-5740,
			"width":360,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"225ff2b0c38f2f6f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The individual behind Rome and their creation of the Christian myth",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-5640,
			"width":360,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ee75d5d1a0e1d958",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"the god of this age; the god of this world",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-5560,
			"width":340,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f8a61f3832e19d68",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"the adversary of humankind",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-5480,
			"width":240,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"429ef2bae519ad74",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Satan / the Devil",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-5400,
			"width":160,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ab408f61ba782b1b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The Beast of Revelation",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-5320,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"fe2261e9c4975fa6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"A physical person",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-5240,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"bb1de6ece5476b72",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Never mentions having a son",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-5140,
			"width":240,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"87204bd797c102bb",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The word God or Lord in the Bible is translated from several different words mainly, Elohim and YHWH. In this study we're going to use the transliteration of the actual Hebrew word that has been translated as God in the Garden of Eden story. That word is Yahweh.\n\nTransliteration means the English-sounding equivalent of the original work in the Hebrew.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-5070,
			"width":420,
			"height":220
		},
		{
			"id":"d190ed7ab0311715",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Elohim",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":440,
			"y":-4980,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"397d5e96d1822b29",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"YHWH",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":440,
			"y":-4800,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"113ba0478d8330cc",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Used from Genesis 1:1 through 2:3",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":580,
			"y":-5100,
			"width":280,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"5d6c8586f6794699",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"-hebrew symbols-",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":580,
			"y":-4960,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"235c4b1b7737b32e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Introduced from Genesis 2:4",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":580,
			"y":-4840,
			"width":240,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a8ba4beb315d283e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"God",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":900,
			"y":-4880,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2ca02fafd09444e5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yahweh",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":900,
			"y":-4810,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"5d97be36a53c0009",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Jehovah",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":900,
			"y":-4740,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"27143047079fe378",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"God",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":900,
			"y":-5220,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"aad5c37af5c5f59d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Gods",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":900,
			"y":-5100,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"913a1b6446d226ff",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Lord",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":900,
			"y":-4960,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"48326292963a9e31",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Elohim is actually plural and most times ought to be translated as \"the gods\". We translate it as \"god\" most of the time, solely due to the Christian narrative of a monotheistic god being such a string influence over translation.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1120,
			"y":-5300,
			"width":460,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"9574ca36f7187ed0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Psalm 82 is a good example of Elohim being translated both as god and the gods in the same sentence.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1120,
			"y":-5140,
			"width":460,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"4ddc402d66eecfaf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"God (elohim) has taken his place in the divine council; in the midst of the gods (elohim) he holds judgment.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1120,
			"y":-5000,
			"width":460,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"01bfd83da6aa749e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"in the cool of the evening, the man and his wife **heard** the Lord God **walking** around in the garden.  So they hid from the Lord God amount the trees in the garden. \n\nThe Lord God called to the man and asked him, \"**Where are you**?\"  \n\nHe answered, \"**I heard you** in the garden. I was afraid because I was naked, so I **hid**.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":480,
			"y":-4400,
			"width":920,
			"height":160
		},
		{
			"id":"b46042e156a972fd",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yahweh is...",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-300,
			"y":-3700,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f950fa7cf3ed7a1d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Where did Satan live?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-320,
			"y":4580,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"06a259ad7ed58766",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"To the messenger of the church in Pergamum, write: The one who holds the sharp two-edged sword says: I know where you live. Satan's throne is there. You hold on to my name and have not denied your belief in me, even in the days of Antipas. He was my faithful witness who was killed in your presence, where Satan lives.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-20,
			"y":4200,
			"width":1180,
			"height":90
		},
		{
			"id":"9653c85bbd816021",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Whose altar is at Pergamum?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-20,
			"y":4380,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a81d5fd64a395bc6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Zeus's",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":300,
			"y":4380,
			"width":90,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a254b5a327bfef4e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What did Zeus do to his father?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":440,
			"y":4380,
			"width":315,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"56eedc7bc179377a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"![[Pasted image 20261018194908.png]]",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-20,
			"y":4580,
			"width":535,
			"height":400
		},
		{
			"id":"c0fd875cfd840e05",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Zeus and Jupiter are the same person",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-20,
			"y":5100,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4dce52ab65d7f1f4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"But Satan's altar is no longer in ...",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-20,
			"y":5300,
			"width":268,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9019bcf4f163da47",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Genesis",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-3820,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a719481c268895af",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"-hebrew symbols-",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":580,
			"y":-4660,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"3ba29e4299c6ece2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The tetragrammaton",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":840,
			"y":-4660,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"0f4bdee6da82b4ab",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yahweh",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":660,
			"y":-4570,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"49eb7e0884454a3b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"According to the entirety of Torah, who is the God of this world?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":320,
			"y":-4580,
			"width":300,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"18882ed6a2528d45",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Who is the God of this world/age?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-4570,
			"width":300,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"d80d02703cf69bd9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Genesis 3:8-10",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1440,
			"y":-4350,
			"width":140,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9210fffad4d1e18a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The the Lord God said, \"The man has become **like one of us**, since he knows good and evil. He must not reach our and take the fruit from the tree of life and eat. Then he would live forever.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":480,
			"y":-4220,
			"width":920,
			"height":85
		},
		{
			"id":"8e176b4b3bbc87ee",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The Garden",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":280,
			"y":-4280,
			"width":130,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"41bab7c0db34d2e0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The Lord **came down to see** the city this is about the tower (of babel) that the descendants of Adam were building.  The Lord said, \"They are one people with one language. This is only the beginning of what they will do! Now nothing they plan to do will be too difficult for them. **Let us go down there** and mix up their language so that they won't understand each other.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":480,
			"y":-4120,
			"width":920,
			"height":85
		},
		{
			"id":"e5c3ec81095904e3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The Lord appeared to Abraham by the oak trees belonging to Mamre as he was sitting at the entrance of his tent during the hottest part of the day. Abraham looked up, and suddenly he saw **three men standing near him**. When he saw them, **he ran to meet them**, and he bowed with his face touching the ground.\n\n\"Please, sir,\" Abraham said, \"stop by to visit me for a while. Why don't we let someone bring a little water? **After you wash your feet you can stretch out and rest under the tree**. Let me bring you some bread that you can regain your strength. After that you can leave, since this is why you stopped by to visit me.\"\n\nThey answered, \"That's fine. Do as you say.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":480,
			"y":-4000,
			"width":920,
			"height":240
		},
		{
			"id":"9a7a6226598c72da",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"So Jacob was left alone then a man wrestled with him until dawn. When the man saw that he could not win against Jacob **he touched the socket of Jacob's hip** so that it was dislocated as they wrestled.\n\nThen the man said, \"**Let me go**; it's almost dawn.\" But Jacob answered, \"**I won't let you go** until you bless me.\"\nSo the man asked him, \"What's your name?\"\n\"Jacob,\" he answered.\nThe man said, \"Your name will no longer be Jacob but Israel \\[He Wrestles With God\\], because you have wrestled with God and with men - and you have won.\"\n\nSo Jacob named that place Peniel \\[Face of God\\], because he said, \"I **have seen God face to face**, but my life was saved.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":480,
			"y":-3740,
			"width":920,
			"height":260
		},
		{
			"id":"66a8de5d8adaa01d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Babel",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":280,
			"y":-4107,
			"width":110,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2703174326075d91",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"...am",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":280,
			"y":-3910,
			"width":110,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a42ec79438552ee6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Genesis 35:9",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":480,
			"y":-3440,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"6ed7b8479391fd60",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"As they left Pharaoh, they found Moses and Aaron waiting for them. So they said, \"May the Lord see what you have done and judge you! You have made Pharaoh and his officials hate us. You have given them an excuse to kill us.\"\n**Moses went back to the Lord** and asked, \"Why have you brought this trouble on your people? Why did you send me? Ever since I went to Pharaoh to speak for you, he had treated your people cruelly, and you have done nothing at all to rescue your people.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":295,
			"y":-3260,
			"width":1105,
			"height":140
		},
		{
			"id":"f8e23aae764a48e5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Genesis 26:2",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":295,
			"y":-3360,
			"width":185,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ae04780497fedfe0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Numbers 12:4-9",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1440,
			"y":-3220,
			"width":185,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"1f5c30c03fc56883",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"As soon as Modes went into the tent, the column of smoke would come down and stay at the entrance to the tent while the Lord spoke with Moses.\n\n**The Lord would speak to Moses personally, as a man speaks to his friend**. Then moses would come back to the camp, but his assistant, Joshua, son of Nun, stayed inside the tent.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":295,
			"y":-3090,
			"width":1105,
			"height":130
		},
		{
			"id":"a509909892c4686f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Exodus",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-3140,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"750a9d0d2ec7bf4a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Chapters 1-7",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":295,
			"y":-2930,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a9bd77eb7f955069",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Suddenly, the Lord said to Moses, Aaron, and Miriam, \"All three of you come to the tent of meeting.\" So all three of them came. Then the Lord came down in the column of smoke and **stood at the entrance to the tent**. He called to Aaron and Miriam, and they both came forward.\nHe said, \"Listen to my words: When there are prophets of the Lord among you, I make myself known to them in visions or speak to them in dreams. But this is not the way I treat my servant Moses. He is the most faithful person in my household. **I speak with him face to face**, plainly and not in riddles. He even sees the form of the Lord. Why weren't you afraid to criticize my servant Moses?\" the Lord was angry with them, **so he left**.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":300,
			"y":-2850,
			"width":1100,
			"height":150
		},
		{
			"id":"482cc2187e9bdbd7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"2 Chronicles",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-2280,
			"width":140,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"0e140b8bbbfce323",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"1 Samuel",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-2180,
			"width":140,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f131088486ea112c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Numbers",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-2805,
			"width":140,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9faeb379948f4481",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Exodus 33",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1440,
			"y":-3055,
			"width":185,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f0074193c9925a14",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"choose a place outside the camp where you can go to relieve yourself. You must carry a pointed stick as part of your equipment. When you go outside to squat, dig a hole with it. When you're done, cover up your excrement. **The Lord your God moves around in your camp** to protect you and hand your enemies over to you. So your camp must always be holy. This way, the Lord will never see anything offensive among you and turn away from you.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":300,
			"y":-2670,
			"width":1100,
			"height":110
		},
		{
			"id":"90da8e7880176568",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Deuteronomy",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-2645,
			"width":140,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"15930a29d3241438",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Deuteronomy",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1440,
			"y":-2645,
			"width":160,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"34971fc9975a1356",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"1 Kings",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-2390,
			"width":140,
			"height":70
		},
		{
			"id":"57e3e196e25e9eae",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Judges",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-2500,
			"width":140,
			"height":70
		},
		{
			"id":"ddec0cdbdc3e9493",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Then Satan stood against Israel and incited David to number Israel. So David said to Joab and the commanders of the army, \"Go, number (or mark) Israel, from Beersheba to Dan, and bring me a report, that i may know their number.\" But Joab said, \"May the LORD add to his people a hundred times as many as they are! Are they not, my lord the king, all of them are my lord's servants? Why then should my lord require this? Why should it be a cause of guilt for Israel?\" But the king's word prevailed against Joab. So Joab departed and went throughout all Israel and came back to Jerusalem. And Joab gave the sum of the numbering of the people to David.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":300,
			"y":-2100,
			"width":1100,
			"height":170
		},
		{
			"id":"865b2fb4d9daba8e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The numbering or the marking of Israel. \nThe same event is recorded twice in the bible.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-2075,
			"width":300,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"1c6b8337eae2171d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"1 Chronicles 21",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1440,
			"y":-2045,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"bc718be655200c53",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The law veils people. Yeshua removes the veil.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-1570,
			"width":380,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2693d48b460a9d31",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"However their minds became closed. In fact to this day the same veil is still there when they read the Old Testament. It isn't removed, because only Christ can remove it. Yet, even today, when they read the books of Moses, a veil covers their minds. But whenever a person turns to the Lord, the veil is taken away.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-1880,
			"width":1180,
			"height":90
		},
		{
			"id":"bb755dd5306f6c60",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"2 Corinthians 3:14-16",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":-1865,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"e0be96b42202e359",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"So if the Good News that we tell others is covered with a veil, it is hidden from those who are dying. The god of this age has blinded the minds of those who don't believe. As a result, they don't see the light of the Good News of Christ's glory. It is Christ who is God's image.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-40,
			"y":-1730,
			"width":1180,
			"height":90
		},
		{
			"id":"1b90fc208f00f5a2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The veil and the unveiling",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-300,
			"y":-1715,
			"width":220,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"8711de89da82cae5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Revalation 2:12-13",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1240,
			"y":4215,
			"width":185,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"5600df8545cd8287",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Genesis 3:22",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1440,
			"y":-4212,
			"width":140,
			"height":70
		},
		{
			"id":"c08d77e4229f4531",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Gen 11:5-7",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1440,
			"y":-4107,
			"width":140,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"1605bf469d5a5ead",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"2 Corinthians 4:3-4",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":-1715,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"138bc401af7c1f7a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What does Apocalypse or Revelation mean? As in, John's Apocalypse / Revelation",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":420,
			"y":-1610,
			"width":655,
			"height":70
		},
		{
			"id":"f92f3673541000ea",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The unveiling!",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":420,
			"y":-1510,
			"width":160,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"98bb5e42e9c1a7ae",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yeshua flees to Egypt??",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":135,
			"y":-1400,
			"width":220,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"83434cb5713b6644",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Deuteronomy 32:48-52",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":-1255,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"56d9a3eaf463f432",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Deuteronomy 34:10",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":-880,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"87cd28133348261d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"That very day Yahweh spoke to Moses, \"Go up this mountain ... which is in the land of Moab, ... and view the land of Canaan, which I am giving to the people of Israel for a possession, and **die on the mountain which you go up** ... because you broke faith with me in the midst of the people of Israel at the waters of Meribah-kadesh, in the wilderness of Zin, and because you did not treat me as holy in the midst of the people of Israel.\n\nFor you shall see the land before you, but you shall not go there, into the land that I am giving to the people of Israel.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":135,
			"y":-1310,
			"width":1005,
			"height":170
		},
		{
			"id":"6816743b5dac566b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Then Moses went up from the plains of Moab to Mount Nebo.  And Yahweh showed him all the land. ... And Yahweh said to him, \"This is the land of which I swore to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob, 'I will give it to your offspring.' I have let you see it with your eyes, but you shall not go over there.\"\n\nSo **Moses the servant of Yahweh died there in the land of Moab**, according to the will of Yahweh, and **he buried him in the valley in the land of Moab**, but no one knows the place of his burial to this day. Moses was 120 years old when he died. His eye was undimmed, and his vigor unabated.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":135,
			"y":-1120,
			"width":1005,
			"height":210
		},
		{
			"id":"61995b90e324b423",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"And there has not arisen a prophet since in Israel like Moses, whom the LORD knew intimately face to face.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":135,
			"y":-880,
			"width":1005,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a8f8a08c5787082a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"When the archangel Michael argued with the devil (Yahweh), they were arguing over the body of Moses. But Michael didn't dare to hand down a judgment against the devil. Instead Michael said, \"May the Lord reprimand you!\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":135,
			"y":-780,
			"width":1005,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"7187e8ba6ed3113d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"When Mikha'el, one of the ruling angels, took issue with the Adversary, arguing over the body of Moshe, he did not dare bring against him an insulting charge, but said, \"May ADONAI rebuke you.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":135,
			"y":-680,
			"width":1005,
			"height":90
		},
		{
			"id":"b4f8c9d737d85e61",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Deuteronomy 34:1-7",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":-1045,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"b694568cc20e2c23",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Stolen from Egypt",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-125,
			"y":-1400,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"fe7094a8ea37778d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yahweh refuses to hand over Moses' body",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-125,
			"y":-730,
			"width":220,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9a8a0e9fb342a3b2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yahweh murders Moses",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-125,
			"y":-1045,
			"width":220,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"5591f59ef03b451f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Moses",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-300,
			"y":-1045,
			"width":110,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2e51142ddf58dbc9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Ruler of this world",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":15,
			"y":195,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f79f0396eefabd2b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Has a Kingdom",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":15,
			"y":345,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ebcc93eb41435c94",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Thief an robber",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":15,
			"y":435,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"cffa4dd431d4dfa9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Destruction of Satan is end of the law",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":15,
			"y":535,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"8c0f0281a369abef",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What does Yeshua say about Satan?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-315,
			"y":70,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2e0bdf9e1d9db225",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"John 14:30",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":255,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"faaa57335dfc8bd4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Matthew 12:26",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":345,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"13eaef56ac5e0804",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"John 10:8",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":435,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"1ba5e81ba94c29c4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Matthew 5",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":535,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2c440bc7f6245bbf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"John 8:41-45",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":-340,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"dee538cc9404676a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Luke 9:51-56",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":-70,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9f550adc31efc9d0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"John 12:31-33",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":130,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"63803ff9727ac2f4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\"This world is being judged now. **The ruler of this world will be thrown out now**. When I have been lifted up from the earth, I will draw all people toward me.\" By saying this, he indicated how he was going to die.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":260,
			"y":115,
			"width":880,
			"height":90
		},
		{
			"id":"89edd59435e9630f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**The rule of this world has no power over me**. But he's coming, so I won't talk with you much longer.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":260,
			"y":255,
			"width":880,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ed19dbb66b81e678",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"If Satan forces Satan out, **he is divided against himself**.\nHow, then, can his kingdom last?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":260,
			"y":335,
			"width":880,
			"height":80
		},
		{
			"id":"fdbd433bfb289776",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**All who came before me** (Yeshua) **are thieves and robbers**.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":260,
			"y":435,
			"width":880,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"d24d9281e1439b19",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Do not think that I have come to abolish the Law or the Prophets; I have not come to abolish them but to fulfill them. For truly, I say to you, until heaven and earth pass away, not an iota, not a dot, will pass from the Law until all is accomplished.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":260,
			"y":515,
			"width":880,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"a415c0c1debd5623",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Your father is the devil",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":15,
			"y":-425,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"3dbd3516d97ac86d",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"\"You're doing what your father does.\"\n\nThe Jews said to Jesus, \"We're not illegitimate children. God is our only Father.\"\n\nJesus told them, \"If God were your Father, you would love me. After all, I'm here, and I came from God. I didn't come on my own. Instead, God sent me. Why don't you understand the language I use? Is it because you can't understand the words I use? **You come from your father, the devil**, and you desire to do what your father wants you to do. **The devil was a murderer from the beginning**. He has never been truthful. He doesn't know what the truth is. Whenever he tells a lie, he's doing what comes naturally to him. **He's a liar and the father of lies**.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":260,
			"y":-425,
			"width":880,
			"height":230
		},
		{
			"id":"9e4b5b09b926f4f0",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Now it came to pass, when the time had come for Him to be received up, that He steadfastly set His face to go to Jerusalem, and sent messengers before His face. And as they went, they entered a village of the Samaritans, to prepare for Him. But they did not receive Him, because His face was set for the journey to Jerusalem. And when His disciple James and John saw this, they said, \"Lord, do You want us to command fire to come down from heaven and consume them, just as Elijah did?\"\nBut He turned and rebuked them, and said, \"**You do not know what manner of spirit you are of**. For the Son of Man did not come to destroy men's lives but to save them.\" And they went to another village.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":260,
			"y":-145,
			"width":880,
			"height":210
		},
		{
			"id":"1e3211c7d5acd95b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Wrong spirit",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":15,
			"y":-70,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"23c9582d75776e07",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"John 8:19",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":-530,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"cc71a2dc5b6c3d35",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The Pharisees asked him, \"Where is your father?\"\n\nJesus replied, \"**You don't know me or my Father**. If you knew me you would also know my Father.\"",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":260,
			"y":-545,
			"width":880,
			"height":90
		},
		{
			"id":"90e351d3e256e214",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"None of the seven letter of Revelation mention the popular notion that Yahweh was Satan",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":58,
			"y":980,
			"width":727,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a3c3ac2b1d48b960",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Why?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":858,
			"y":980,
			"width":95,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"b45dcf0ba0a78f35",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"You were once dead because of your failures and sins. You followed the ways of this present world and its spiritual ruler. This ruler continues to work in people who refuse to obey God. All of us once lived among these people, and followed the desires of our corrupt nature.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":260,
			"y":660,
			"width":880,
			"height":110
		},
		{
			"id":"9fb742944d160c99",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"your adversary the devil prowls around like a roaring lion seeking someone to devour",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":260,
			"y":780,
			"width":880,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"89cc837f1e79da83",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The reason that the Son of God appeared was to destroy what the devil does",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":260,
			"y":870,
			"width":880,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a5f8cf541d6ab7fc",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"1 Peter 3:8",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":780,
			"width":135,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"8ba2c4eff7f4b5e4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"1 John 3:8",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1200,
			"y":870,
			"width":135,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"cd768c71c0849add",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Paul",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":58,
			"y":685,
			"width":115,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"0856a7b681e182aa",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Peter",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":58,
			"y":780,
			"width":115,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2b0ec879d710b3a3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Other texts",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-315,
			"y":810,
			"width":130,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"0357da409a89a958",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"John",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":58,
			"y":870,
			"width":115,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"0ee41c67de36d21e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"zeus overthrew his father chronos to become the new god of the greek pantheon",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":318,
			"y":5100,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"294088993ff42aac",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Post-snake",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":225,
			"y":1660,
			"width":140,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"3cf4165dc65112f9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Has self awareness",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":1640,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"bc0655992c5368fe",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Access to all the fruit in the garden",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":1720,
			"width":300,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4e2996e75d5bf6b5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Biological immortality",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":1800,
			"width":210,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"699eb6057b87cfb5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Man is in the garden",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":1560,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"a9f3046c98e6afb9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Cursed & Restored",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":5,
			"y":1930,
			"width":180,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ef02825c3139205f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yahweh curses mankind and their relationship with the snake",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":1960,
			"width":500,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"c12bea044fdbc4ab",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Post Yahweh's curse",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":225,
			"y":2020,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"9f6a869b39ea9ab5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"No curse",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":1880,
			"width":120,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"1bdc2778bf91f707",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"No access to any of the fruit of the garden",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2200,
			"width":340,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"92fb5aeab34e3e0e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Man is now outside of the garden",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2040,
			"width":300,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"651740e7a85dd84a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"No biological immortality",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2280,
			"width":250,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"eef35be2e2c352aa",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"He still has self-awareness",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2120,
			"width":250,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"81e5a5364f63e067",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Man is in the garden",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":1120,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"619c260451776472",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yahweh didn't want Adam & Eve to be able to recognize good from evil.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":858,
			"y":1150,
			"width":400,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"5bf12aae6a8407a7",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"No self-awareness",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":1200,
			"width":185,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2feaa320ed55c748",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Unlike Yahweh, who could",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":858,
			"y":1230,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"cf7387216391492f",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Pre-snake",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":225,
			"y":1280,
			"width":140,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f82fbc469bd304e6",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Access to all the trees except the tree of good and evil.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":1320,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"e2ad9d175db11fc9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Biological immortality\n(because they had access to the fruit of the tree)",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":1400,
			"width":420,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"e5e4cc07eb4bae7a",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"No curse",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":1480,
			"width":120,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4d14e28af826c3b9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"No curse",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2710,
			"width":130,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"3c4dac9e522d0c98",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Summary",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":225,
			"y":2890,
			"width":140,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"ea1e1b0b9160a3c3",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"If the snake in the garden is Satan, one is forced to explain why Yeshua in Revelation 22 is restoring mankind back to the state that Satan wanted for them in the garden, AND why the text calls it a restoration.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":318,
			"y":3140,
			"width":570,
			"height":90
		},
		{
			"id":"35bedb01fec6a8c2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The theological dilemma",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":25,
			"y":3155,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"cae6236069d25cab",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What the snake wanted for man",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2790,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"3a1a53c35a64cf00",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What Yahweh did to us",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2890,
			"width":235,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"b1bae4a1678fcc83",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What Yeshua restores to us",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2970,
			"width":235,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"aa17dae911dd38cd",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Cursed us to die by cutting off access to the fruit of the trees.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":805,
			"y":2890,
			"width":380,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"46eac72fb4cfb81c",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Free access to the fruit of all the trees.\nTo live forever.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":825,
			"y":2970,
			"width":360,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"8ee1f8477eb3375b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Free access to the fruit of all the trees.\nTo live forever.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":845,
			"y":2790,
			"width":340,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f32d793d83538c97",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Jesus, whom heaven must receive until the time for restoring all the things about which God spoke.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":925,
			"y":3070,
			"width":540,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"b7ff1de75a974271",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"The only **previous state** that Yeshua is **restoring**, is the one the **snake created** before Yahweh cursed them.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":925,
			"y":3155,
			"width":540,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"c25f3594377ed5aa",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"This is an obvious theological dilemma that you've never been taught, because it's immediately obvious that the snake simply can't be Satan, and the entire Christian narrative will collapse as its foundation of original sin and the snake being Satan, evaporates.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":925,
			"y":3245,
			"width":540,
			"height":120
		},
		{
			"id":"55f37c2a17399048",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Reframing the context",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":25,
			"y":3630,
			"width":220,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f50624cee9163ff8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Christianity (says)",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":315,
			"y":3450,
			"width":170,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"4818c8176b2c12aa",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Bible",
			"styleAttributes":{"textAlign":"center"},
			"x":318,
			"y":3720,
			"width":85,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"3cce4b0faba3f000",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"(that's) God in the garden",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":535,
			"y":3390,
			"width":145,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"49c2cf48cd0135da",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Snake",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":535,
			"y":3530,
			"width":90,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"59fda5b11b316f14",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yahweh",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":535,
			"y":3610,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"e6f6363df5f3af89",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"God the creator of mankind",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":705,
			"y":3390,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"8fd6d27a9447122e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Satan, a fallen angel",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":705,
			"y":3530,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"91b4e9d34996e6a9",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Ruler of the Garden of Eden",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":705,
			"y":3610,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"06213c9775b69ced",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"**God of this world** according to the entirety of Torah.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":705,
			"y":3690,
			"width":300,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"db939768b19ab8cf",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"But not THE God.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1045,
			"y":3690,
			"width":170,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"0fd1608628f42521",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Snake",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":535,
			"y":3810,
			"width":100,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"47c78bd952cff93b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Yeshua, the creator of mankind",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":705,
			"y":3810,
			"width":300,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"960f382cc292707e",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Created the desired state for mankind that Yahweh then destroys.  Yeshua then restores us to that state again in Revelation 22.",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":1045,
			"y":3790,
			"width":420,
			"height":100
		},
		{
			"id":"fca98ff0a3ef3af8",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Restored by Yeshua",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":225,
			"y":2400,
			"width":200,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"1889514b9abbd680",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"What really happened in the garden?",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":-315,
			"y":2630,
			"width":260,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"f7c4be7fd86c4595",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Man is in the garden",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2380,
			"width":210,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"6494865362cfbc4b",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Has self-awareness",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2460,
			"width":210,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"2d9dd243f2bf0fe4",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Access to all the fruit in the garden",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2550,
			"width":300,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"53a447e836eb4fd5",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"Biological immortality",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":485,
			"y":2630,
			"width":210,
			"height":60
		},
		{
			"id":"6dfb8c768daa28ed",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"![[Pasted image 20261018195133.png]]",
			"styleAttributes":{},
			"x":600,
			"y":4630,
			"width":560,
			"height":300
		}
